        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "119ecbac-43ed-554a-9f16-482edbedbe6d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nathaniel Fillmore Jr., Millard Fillmore, Mary Abigail \"Abbie\" Powers Fillmore, Zachary Taylor, Abigail Powers\n- Roles: American farmer, U.S. Representative from New York, Vice President of the United States, President of the United States, daughter of a president\n\nFacts:\n- Nathaniel Fillmore Jr. was born on April 19, 1771, and he was an American farmer.\n- Millard Fillmore was a former U.S. Representative from New York.\n- Millard Fillmore was elected the 12th Vice President of the United States in 1848.\n- Millard Fillmore became President of the United States after the death of Zachary Taylor.\n- Mary Abigail \"Abbie\" Powers Fillmore was born in Buffalo, New York, on March 27, 1832.\n- Nathaniel Fillmore Jr. was the father of Millard Fillmore, who became the 13th President of the United States.\n- Mary Abigail \"Abbie\" Powers Fillmore was the daughter of President Millard Fillmore and Abigail Powers.\n- Mary Abigail \"Abbie\" Powers Fillmore died in East Aurora, New York, on July 26, 1854.\n- Nathaniel Fillmore Jr. died on March 28, 1863.",
